    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4d30e8ed-ba40-45a6-b96b-fda3ed12cc9b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201650323869_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Med Surg Nursing Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-07\n\nLocation: Salem\n\nMISSION:  To educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ.  Nursing: This pool accepts applications for potential openings for part-time instructors (adjuncts) that may arise throughout the year and is not a guarantee of an open position. Adjuncts for the nursing program have historically taught sections of theory, lab, and/or clinical.   QUALIFICATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS :   Education: A master’s degree in nursing is required to teach theory. Exhibit expertise (either work or research) in the discipline to be taught. Applicants teaching clinical need an Oregon State Nursing License. Prior teaching experience preferred.  ESSENTIAL DUTIES:   Develop course schedules and syllabi. Identify and meet the learning needs of students. Supervise students in the clinical setting. Perform Biblical Integration in line with Corban’s Statement of Faith. Develop and administer formative and summative assessment instruments for students’ progress and competence. Work closely and maintain consistent communication with Nursing program faculty.   Character: The candidate must have a personal relationship with Jesus Christ and evidence a mature Christian faith, be in agreement with the University’s Statement of Faith, and be committed to the integration of biblical principles within the discipline of nursing.     Faculty Overview Corban University is a Christian university whose purpose is to educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ.  The university is accredited by the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities.   Corban provides a strong Bible-centered academic program with more than 50 majors and programs of study including professional, liberal arts, and ministries. Along with traditional and adult degree completion programs at the undergraduate level, Corban offers graduate teacher licensure programs and graduate degrees in education, business, counseling, and ministry.  A personal relationship with Jesus Christ is a requirement for all employees and students.   Within these guidelines, it is our policy to provide equal opportunity to all applicants, employees and students and to not discriminate on the basis of gender, disability, race, color, national origin or age in access to, or treatment in employment.   Institutional Statement Corban University is a private comprehensive university of liberal arts, ministry, and professional studies with a mission to educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ. All employees are expected to model servant leadership in all aspects of their work. Corban values and recruits for a workforce that is diverse in gender, age, ethnicity, race, and/or ability, and seeks employees who will interact with the Corban community in a way that reflects a commitment to cultural proficiency. Where permitted by law and consistent with the school’s history, mission, and core values, Corban exercises religious preference throughout the University. Employees must have a personal relationship with Jesus Christ, agree with the University Statement of Faith, evidence a mature Christian faith, and be an active member of a Bible-believing, Gospel-preaching local church.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4d30e8ed-ba40-45a6-b96b-fda3ed12cc9b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201659242379_3&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Help Desk Lead Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-24\n\nLocation: Salem\n\nMISSION:  To educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ.  SUMMARY: To provide timely, quality service to end user requests; monitor helpdesk tickets, participate in computer replacement cycle, software and hardware upgrades for all end user and classroom computers and technologies.  ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: The Help Desk Lead Technician works directly with university employees to support their efforts to educate students and related activities.  In this role, they will: Provide input regarding end user computer replacement process. Document and maintain inventory of all end user computers and software licenses. Document and manage FAQ/Wiki with technical support information for helpdesk employees. Assist users with software, hardware, phone, network and communication problems. Support users with Microsoft Windows and Apple devices and setup and manage network access of Corban owned devices. Support mobile users and their devices including laptops, tablets, and cell phones.  Provide support for all classroom technologies. Provide excellent customer service to employees and students by quickly answering and returning phone calls, and by responding to issues and tickets as received, acknowledging receipt and providing a timeline for completion. Provide support for all Office 365 applications. Create and maintain user accounts in AD and Entra environments. Maintain a current knowledge of computer systems, practices and policies. Maintain the highest ethical standard regarding software, software sharing and computer usage in compliance with the University’s Acceptable Usage Policy and Employee Handbook. Support the university-wide efforts to recruit and retain students. Perform other duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:  Proven interpersonal, written, verbal, and listening skills.  Highly self-motivated and directed. Strong customer service orientation.  Be able to work as a contributing member of a group, and individually when necessary with a strong sense of accountability and good decision-making skills. Understanding of permissions and management of Active Directory and Azure AD. Understanding of networking and supporting Mac OS in a Microsoft environment. Solid and demonstrated understanding and support of VoIP systems. Solid understanding and support of multifunctional printers; configuration and setup, management, and support. Ability to manage competing priorities, multiple, simultaneous projects, and logically perform troubleshooting tasks to arrive at effective solutions. Technology best practices and data security. Maintain integrity and confidentiality regarding internal Corban data. Ability to respond to common inquiries or complaints from users and campus guests. Ability to effectively present information to public groups. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office. Ability to read log files, manipulate data, and create reports.  QUALIFICATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS:    Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution is preferred.  Candidate must be a customer service-oriented personality who enjoys interacting with people.  Proficient with Microsoft Office, Apple iWork (Pages, Numbers, and Keynote), Google Apps. Proficient with IT analytical tools and applications. Demonstrated understanding of DNS and DHCP, implementation, and troubleshooting. Ability to work with well with non-technical customers and explain complex technical concepts. Evangelical Christian commitment and lifestyle consistent with the university’s mission as described in our Statement of Faith Candidates should value an environment that reflects the diversity of God’s kingdom, engages in global concerns and connects culturally. Professional dress and cleanliness in-line with the culture of a Christian institution of higher education is required.  WORKING CONDITIONS:  PHYSICAL DEMANDS:  While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; walk; use hand to finger, handle, or feel objects, tools, or controls; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; and talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. The job requires sitting for extended periods of time. The Employee must frequently lift and/or move up to 25 pounds and occasionally lift and/or more up to 50 pounds. Specific visual abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. WORK ENVIRONMENT:  The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee occasionally works near moving mechanical parts; in high, precarious places; and in outside weather conditions and is occasionally exposed to cold, heat, risk of electrical shock, risk of radiation and vibration. Occasional evening and weekend work to may be required to meet deadlines.     Corban University is a private, co-educational, university of liberal arts, ministry and professional studies with a mission to educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ. All employees are expected to model servant leadership to customers, including o ther employees, students and the public. Corban values and encourages qualified applicants who are diverse in gender, age, ethnicity, race and/or ability, and seeks candidates who will interact with the Corban community in a way that reflects a commitment to cultural proficiency. Where permitted by law and consistent with the school’s history, mission and core values, Corban exercises religious preference throughout the University. Candidates must have a personal relationship with Jesus Christ, evidence a mature Christian faith and be an active member in a local church.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4d30e8ed-ba40-45a6-b96b-fda3ed12cc9b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201659236831_4&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Director of Online and Adult Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-25\n\nLocation: Salem\n\nMISSION:  To educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ.  PURPOSE: Grow, manage, and direct the Corban University online program.   SUMMARY: The primary function of the Director of Online and Adult Studies is to grow enrollment in its existing online degree programs, help adult learners persist to graduation, and increase sustainable net tuition revenue. The director will lead the unit’s growth and day-to-day operations, working with Admissions and Academic Affairs to turn enrollment goals into action within the first year.  ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS  The major responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Grow enrollment.  Develop and execute a recruitment strategy for adult learners, including returning Corban students, transfer students, and working adults with prior college credit. Partner with Admissions and Marketing to improve outreach, follow-up, and conversion from inquiry to enrollment. Build recruitment partnerships.  Develop relationships with employers, churches, community colleges, and other organizations that can refer students or support their education. Evaluate partnerships by the enrollments they generate and the cost of serving those students. Improve the student experience.  Work with Admissions, the Registrar, Financial Aid, and academic leaders to help prospective students understand how their credits transfer, what their degree will cost, and how long it will take to finish. Coordinate onboarding, advising, and early outreach to students at risk of stopping out. Coordinate academic delivery.  Partner with academic leaders and the Assistant Director of Online to align course schedules and staffing with student demand, maintain academic quality, and ensure students can access required courses in the sequence they need to graduate. Build and lead the team.  Assess staffing needs, clarify responsibilities across the unit and its campus partners, coach staff, and recommend staffing changes as enrollment grows. Manage financial performance.  Track net tuition revenue, recruitment costs, and direct program expenses with Finance. Use those results to guide spending and recommend where Corban should invest, adjust, or discontinue recruitment efforts. QUALIFICATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS:  Master’s degree required. MBA or Ph.D. preferred. Minimum of 3 years of progressive responsible professional work experience working with students in an academic environment. Experience leading a program, team, or business initiative with measurable responsibility for growth or operating results. Experience serving adult learners, transfer students, or online students. Ability to use enrollment, customer, or financial data to set priorities and manage performance. Demonstrated ability to collaborate across departments and improve the experience of the people the program serves. Entrepreneurial experience preferred, such as starting a business, launching a new program or unit, or leading another imitative that required significant creativity and working in a complex market. Bilingual in English and Spanish preferred. Candidates must have a personal relationship with Jesus Christ and evidence a mature Christian faith, be in agreement with the University’s Statement of Faith (www.corban.edu/about/statementof-faith) and employee lifestyle standards, be committed and articulate in the integration of biblical principles within the Advancement profession and be willing to invest themselves in the success of Corban University. WORKING CONDITIONS: Most work will be conducted from the campus of Corban University, but some travel as well as some evening and weekend work may be required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  Corban University is a private comprehensive university of liberal arts, ministry, and professional studies with a mission to educate Christians who will make a difference in the world for Jesus Christ. All employees are expected to model servant leadership in all aspects of their work. Corban values and recruits for a workforce that is diverse in gender, age, ethnicity, race, and/or ability, and seeks employees who will interact with the Corban community in a way that reflects a commitment to cultural proficiency. Where permitted by law and consistent with the school’s history, mission, and core values, Corban exercises religious preference throughout the University. Employees must have a personal relationship with Jesus Christ, agree with the University Statement of Faith, evidence a mature Christian faith, and be an active member of a Bible-believing, Gospel-preaching local church.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
